nodecode-protonmail is a rewrite of Maytrella007's Maytrella007/hermes-proton:

  https://github.com/Maytrella007/hermes-proton
  commit 3e0612848cf20116294f9ff58e74aadf34bc858e

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 William Wilamo (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the sign-in, the read side and the send path of the mail
API, in Common Lisp instead of Python. The cell speaks Proton's own `/auth/v4`,
`/core/v4` and `/mail/v4` endpoints with `nlk:http`; the SRP-6a handshake, its
little-endian big integers and its expand-hash, and the bcrypt underneath it
are ported from the original's `protonlite/srp.py`, with Blowfish's constants
read from the copy ironclad already carries. Body decryption and encryption are
handed to the machine's `gpg` on a throwaway keyring rather than to a bundled
PGP library, so the OpenPGP framing the send API wants -- the literal packet,
the signature, splitting gpg's output into one key packet per recipient and the
data packet, and reading the session key back for the recipients outside Proton
-- is in `send.lisp`; the HTML-to-prose step is much smaller than the
original's.

What was left out: drafts kept on the server, labels and moves, contacts,
calendar and Drive, the saved session file, the CLI, inline and uploaded
attachments on the send side, and the signature check on the server's SRP
modulus (the cell checks its size and the ephemeral's bounds, and relies on TLS
for the rest).
